search_source_create_chunks = Split into sections
search_source_create_chunks_notice = The basis of the semantic search. Every section later gets a vector – that costs one call to the AI service and about 6 KB in the database. Think twice for document sources: eight PDFs can yield more sections than two hundred articles.
search_source_chunk_strategy = Splitting
search_chunk_whole = Whole document
search_chunk_whole_description = one section per record, undivided – for short content such as YForm records and metadata
search_chunk_fixed = Fixed size
search_chunk_fixed_description = pieces of a fixed length with overlap, cut at paragraph and sentence boundaries
search_chunk_markdown = By outline
search_chunk_markdown_description = along the headings, every section remembers its heading path; without an outline it behaves like "Fixed size"
search_chunk_size = Section size in characters
search_chunk_size_notice = A target, not a limit – a paragraph is not torn apart just because it runs a few characters over. 800 to 2000 are sensible.
search_chunk_overlap = Overlap in characters
search_chunk_overlap_notice = This much of the end of the previous section starts the next one, so a sentence on the boundary is not lost. 0 switches it off.
search_chunk_merge_below = Merge small sections
search_chunk_merge_below_notice = A section shorter than this many characters is merged into the following one – a heading with a single sentence under it is not a section of its own. 0 switches merging off. Sections are only merged while the result still fits the section size.
search_source_collect_words = Collect words for suggestions
search_source_collect_words_notice = Contributes this source's words to partial matches and spelling correction. Sensibly off for document sources: scanned PDFs bring along plenty of character sequences that are not words.
